<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gao</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gao is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger River</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>. It was absorbed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> and later became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>, which rose to dominate the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sudan">western Sudan</a>. It is home to the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askia-muhammad">Askia Muhammad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gao.jpg" alt="Gao" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Sessoms from Fribourg, Switzerland · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tombeau_dAskia_in_Gao_by_David_Sessoms.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
